WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.292
Before any object moves, decompose
the AD identity model into its parts,

2
00:00:05.292 --> 00:00:07.425
because each has its own path.

3
00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:10.662
OUs do three jobs, and each
goes somewhere different.

4
00:00:10.662 --> 00:00:15.302
Group Policy scoping becomes
Conditional Access and Intune profiles,

5
00:00:15.302 --> 00:00:18.212
targeted by group
membership, not container.

6
00:00:18.212 --> 00:00:21.916
Administrative delegation
becomes administrative units,

7
00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:26.212
which are free to create, though each
AU-scoped administrator needs P1.

8
00:00:26.212 --> 00:00:30.324
Logical organization becomes
dynamic groups and attributes.

9
00:00:30.324 --> 00:00:35.301
The forest maps to the tenant: one trust
boundary, no domain trusts inside it,

10
00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:39.875
and verified domains are routing
suffixes, not security boundaries.

11
00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:43.800
Trusts become B2B and
cross-tenant access settings.

12
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.804
AdminSDHolder has no equivalent;
Privileged Identity Management,

13
00:00:47.804 --> 00:00:52.094
which makes assignments eligible and
time-bound, and protected actions,

14
00:00:52.094 --> 00:00:55.669
which demand an authentication
context before high-impact

15
00:00:55.669 --> 00:00:58.600
permissions are used,
together serve its purpose.

16
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.550
And Schema Admins has none:
Microsoft manages the schema.

17
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:07.112
This is the design principle: Entra
ID inverts the governance model.

18
00:01:07.112 --> 00:01:11.174
Attributes decide memberships,
and memberships decide policy.

19
00:01:11.174 --> 00:01:14.200
That's why attribute quality
gates everything after it.

20
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.537
Licensing gates the governance features.

21
00:01:16.537 --> 00:01:18.700
Conditional Access needs P1.

22
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.825
Dynamic groups need P1 per unique member.

23
00:01:21.825 --> 00:01:26.950
PIM, including PIM for Groups, and
risk-based Conditional Access need P2.

24
00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:31.956
As of October 2026, access reviews and
entitlement management need Entra ID

25
00:01:31.956 --> 00:01:34.737
Governance for the member users involved,

26
00:01:34.737 --> 00:01:40.300
with only some capabilities left under P2,
and Lifecycle Workflows need Governance.

27
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.140
Conditional Access for
workload identities is

28
00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.050
a separate Workload
Identities Premium license.

29
00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:51.150
The chapters assume P2 for everyone and
Governance for the governed populations.

30
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:57.150
One date to act on: the preview
member-of operator ends November 3, 2026.

31
00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.387
After that, dynamic groups,
dynamic administrative

32
00:02:00.387 --> 00:02:03.775
units and auto-assignment
policies that use it freeze.

33
00:02:03.775 --> 00:02:05.330
Replace those rules now.
